---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy information for Church Software UK, including current analytics, form and structured-data practices."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Privacy" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: 27 July 2026.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to accept analytics cookies, the site uses Google
        Analytics 4 to understand general site use and whether visitors follow
        a supplier link from a software profile. Google
        Analytics may set or read analytics cookies and process technical data
        such as IP address, browser and device information, pages viewed and
        event information. A supplier-link event records the supplier name, not
        information entered by a visitor.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google processes this information under its own privacy terms. Do not
        provide personal, church-member, pastoral, safeguarding or financial
        information through the site or in URLs.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can reject analytics cookies in the banner or change your choice at
        any time through the Cookie settings button shown on every page.
      </p>

      <h2>Public contribution routes</h2>
      <p>
        Software suggestions and supplier updates open an email addressed to
        <a href="mailto:directory@churchsoftware.co.uk">directory@churchsoftware.co.uk</a>.
        The site does not receive or store the message content.
      </p>
      <p>Your email provider and the provider for the directory mailbox process messages under their own terms. Do not include church-member, pastoral, safeguarding, financial or other sensitive information. Submit only public supplier evidence and, if needed, business contact details. Maintainers use messages to assess factual corrections or research leads independently; an email does not guarantee publication or a particular editorial outcome.</p>

      <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
      <p>
        The configured production domain is served through Cloudflare, checked on
        25 July 2026. No responsible publisher or final privacy contact is
        configured, so the site is not ready for public launch. Routine hosting
        may process information such as IP addresses, browser details and
        timestamps for security and service operation.
      </p>

      <h2>Public software data</h2>
      <p>
        The structured export contains publishable product information and public
        supplier-source URLs. It does not contain private editorial notes or user
        submissions.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and questions</h2>
      <p>
        If a responsible publisher or contact route is configured, this notice
        will be updated with a way to request access or deletion for directory
        emails. Until then, please avoid
        sending personal or sensitive information through the project’s public
        routes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
